1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,770
Most people pay bank

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,470
and investment fees every month without noticing.

3
00:00:04,490 --> 00:00:05,930
Each one is small.

4
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:07,200
Together, they're not.

5
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,860
This video goes through every type of fee,

6
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,890
from your bank account

7
00:00:11,910 --> 00:00:13,700
and your card to your investments.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,300
Almost all of them fit into ten boxes.

9
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,310
Some you can avoid with one click.

10
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:21,760
Some are capped by law.

11
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,390
And some are hidden on purpose.

12
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,180
Prices vary by bank and by country.

13
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,750
No brand names here,

14
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,640
and this is not financial advice.

15
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:33,600
Let's open the first box.

16
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:35,530
Box 1.

17
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:36,590
Account fees.

18
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,720
Many traditional banks charge a monthly fee just

19
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,100
to keep your account open,

20
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,690
often bundled with services you never use.

21
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:46,670
A few euros

22
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:48,470
a month doesn't feel like much.

23
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,860
But €8 a month

24
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,430
is almost €100 a year, every year.

25
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:55,200
Many online banks offer

26
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:56,850
a basic account for free.

27
00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:59,300
It's one of the easiest savings there is.

28
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,340
And switching

29
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:02,940
is easier than it used to be.

30
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,390
Under EU rules,

31
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:06,230
your new bank must offer a switching service

32
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:08,040
that moves your payments for you.

33
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:10,010
Box 2.

34
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:10,910
Card fees.

35
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,070
Your bank card

36
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:14,500
can come with a yearly fee,

37
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,430
and a premium card costs more,

38
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:17,930
with insurance and perks.

39
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,470
The question is simple:

40
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:22,300
do you actually use those perks?

41
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,070
If not, you're paying for a logo.

42
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:27,170
For most daily payments,

43
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:28,360
a basic debit card is enough.

44
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:32,390
And many people pay for travel insurance twice:

45
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,680
once with their card, and once separately.

46
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:36,710
Box 3.

47
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:37,870
Overdraft fees.

48
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:41,330
Going below zero is one of the most

49
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:43,270
expensive things you can do at a bank.

50
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:46,020
Interest, plus a fee for every incident.

51
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:49,930
In France, the law caps these incident fees

52
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:52,900
at €8 per operation and €80 a month.

53
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:55,070
Many banks charge the maximum.

54
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:58,040
A small buffer on your account

55
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:00,250
is often the cheapest way to avoid them.

56
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:04,140
And remember, even an authorised overdraft

57
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:04,830
is a loan,

58
00:02:04,850 --> 00:02:06,640
often at a high interest rate.

59
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:08,600
Box 4.

60
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:09,700
Currency fees.

61
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,860
Pay by card in another currency,

62
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,800
and your bank converts the money.

63
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:15,960
Many add a markup

64
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:17,670
on top of the exchange rate.

65
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:20,730
Since 2020, EU banks

66
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,570
must show you that markup,

67
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:25,090
compared with the European Central Bank's rate.

68
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,560
Some cards charge no markup at all.

69
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:29,450
On a trip abroad,

70
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:31,130
the difference adds up fast.

71
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:33,660
The same thing happens

72
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,150
when you buy foreign shares.

73
00:02:35,170 --> 00:02:36,750
Your broker may add a markup

74
00:02:36,770 --> 00:02:38,290
when it converts your euros.

75
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,080
Box 5.

76
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:41,940
The question at the cash machine.

77
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:44,680
Abroad, a card machine

78
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:46,000
or an ATM may ask:

79
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,630
pay in euros, or in the local currency?

80
00:02:48,650 --> 00:02:49,780
It sounds helpful.

81
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:52,350
It usually isn't.

82
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:53,980
Choosing your home currency lets

83
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,310
the machine pick the exchange rate,

84
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:57,640
and it's rarely a good one.

85
00:02:58,930 --> 00:03:02,380
A Norwegian bank checked 1,500 withdrawals abroad.

86
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,210
Choosing the home currency cost

87
00:03:04,230 --> 00:03:07,040
more in 99.7% of cases.

88
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,660
The rule consumer groups give is simple:

89
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,300
pay in the local currency.

90
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,240
Box 6.

91
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,400
Transfer fees.

92
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,410
Sending euros to another EU country must cost

93
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,340
the same as sending them at home.

94
00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:25,560
And since 2025, in the euro area,

95
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,190
an instant transfer can't cost

96
00:03:27,210 --> 00:03:28,580
more than a normal one.

97
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,780
Outside the euro, it's different.

98
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:35,000
International transfers can carry fees on both sides,

99
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,360
plus a currency markup.

100
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:39,760
And since October 2025,

101
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,520
your bank checks that the name

102
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:43,430
matches the account before you send.

103
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:45,520
It's called verification of payee.

104
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:47,630
Box 7.

105
00:03:47,650 --> 00:03:48,470
Fund fees.

106
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,830
Every fund charges a yearly fee,

107
00:03:51,850 --> 00:03:53,710
taken quietly from its value.

108
00:03:53,730 --> 00:03:54,940
You never see a bill.

109
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:57,520
A world index ETF

110
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:00,610
can cost around 0.2% a year.

111
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:04,080
Many bank funds charge 1.5% or more.

112
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,560
Over decades, that gap compounds,

113
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,110
and it can eat

114
00:04:08,130 --> 00:04:09,710
a large part of your gains.

115
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,480
In Europe, every fund sold

116
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:15,080
to the public has a key information document

117
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,280
that shows its costs.

118
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,500
The cost section is worth two minutes.

119
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,580
Box 8.

120
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:21,480
Entry fees.

121
00:04:22,770 --> 00:04:23,390
Some funds

122
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:26,060
and insurance contracts charge an entry fee,

123
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:26,780
a few percent

124
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,250
of every euro you put in.

125
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,320
With a 3% entry fee,

126
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:35,790
€1,000 becomes €970 the moment you invest.

127
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,220
Entry fees are often negotiable,

128
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,550
and many online platforms

129
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:42,070
don't charge them at all.

130
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:45,850
Some funds also charge an exit fee,

131
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:46,740
or a performance fee

132
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,210
when they beat a target.

133
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:50,200
Box 9.

134
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:51,170
Broker fees.

135
00:04:52,470 --> 00:04:54,270
Brokers can charge per trade,

136
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:55,840
every year for custody,

137
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:57,260
and for converting currency

138
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,960
when you buy foreign shares.

139
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:02,610
Some even charge an inactivity fee.

140
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:04,000
You pay for doing nothing.

141
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:07,030
Some fees are capped by law.

142
00:05:07,050 --> 00:05:08,740
On a French PEA,

143
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:11,790
custody fees are capped at 0.4% a year,

144
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:14,620
and online trades at 0.5%.

145
00:05:15,930 --> 00:05:17,450
Before choosing a broker,

146
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:18,810
look at the full price list,

147
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:20,480
not just the price of a trade.

148
00:05:21,770 --> 00:05:22,340
Box 10.

149
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,330
Free trading.

150
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:26,950
Zero commission apps still earn money.

151
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,430
Often through the spread,

152
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:29,460
the gap between the buy

153
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,540
and the sell price.

154
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:34,310
Some also earned money by sending your orders

155
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:35,280
to a trading firm

156
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,370
that paid them for it.

157
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:38,500
That's called payment for order flow.

158
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,100
The EU banned it.

159
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:44,850
The last national exceptions ended in June 2026.

160
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:47,790
A wide spread on every trade

161
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:50,360
can cost more than a small, honest commission.

162
00:05:51,670 --> 00:05:54,030
Free usually means you pay somewhere else.

163
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:55,680
It's worth finding out where.

164
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,830
Those are the ten fee boxes.

165
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:00,680
Check your last bank statement.

166
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,590
You'll probably find two or three of them.

167
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,530
Once a year, list what you pay:

168
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:07,840
account, card, funds, broker.

169
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,430
Then cut what you don't use.

170
00:06:10,730 --> 00:06:13,310
Prices change, and every bank is different.

171
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:15,340
This is not financial advice.

172
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:18,240
Small fees, paid every month,

173
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,890
for decades, are never small.

174
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,420
And every fee you cut

175
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,190
is a return you get, guaranteed.

176
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,060
If this helped, subscribe.

177
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,710
Next up, every investing mistake, explained.

